DESCRIPTION >
    Leads: single-visitor detail (first/last seen, pageview+conversion
    counts, revenue, first-touch attribution fields, active days). Tenant-
    scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp). Faithful 1:1 port of
    api/routes/leads-server.js:224-245 (queryName 'lead_detail'). Identity
    rule #19a: WHERE distinct_id = <param>, canonical stitching key.
    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id ->
    site_id, event -> event_type, properties.utm_source -> utm_source
    (Nullable), properties.first_touch_source -> first_touch_source
    (DEFAULT 'direct'), properties.utm_medium -> utm_medium (Nullable),
    properties.first_touch_medium -> first_touch_medium (DEFAULT 'none'),
    properties.ai_source -> ai_source (Nullable), properties.country ->
    country (Nullable), properties.page_url -> page_url (Nullable),
    properties.conversion_value -> conversion_value (Float64 DEFAULT 0).
    toFloatOrZero -> toFloat64OrZero (same class of fix as prior batches).
    §7 NULL-SKIP ANALYSIS — same per-field conclusions as leads_list.pipe
    (full table + evidence in the batch dispatch report): source/medium/
    ai_source are COALESCE-guarded (never skip, no fix needed); country/
    first_page_url are genuinely Nullable typed columns (skip already
    matches live HogQL, no fix needed).
    THIS PIPE ADDS TWO RAW (non-COALESCE) argMin fields not present in
    leads_list: argMin(properties.first_touch_source) and
    argMin(properties.first_touch_medium) — both DEFAULT-backed typed
    columns ('direct'/'none'). A nullIf(...) null-skip restoration was
    tried for these plus campaign, then REJECTED after live cross-store
    testing on cc-4c-visitorY: live HogQL resolves
    campaign=''/first_touch_source='direct'/first_touch_medium='none' (real,
    explicitly-set values, not absent) for every event this pipe will ever
    see in Tinybird — the only genuinely-NULL rows for these fields on the
    gating site (439/459) come from `demo_run3_user_*` bulk/offline-seeded
    data (ingestion_method NULL/'offline') that bypasses the live tracker
    pipeline, predates the dual-write cutover, and is absent from Tinybird
    by construction. Applying nullIf(x, DEFAULT) nulled out the real
    resolved values instead, a verified regression (live: campaign=''
    /fts='direct'/ftm='none'; nullIf'd typed side: all NULL — mismatch).
    Left as plain column references. Output column names are ft_source /
    ft_medium (not first_touch_source/first_touch_medium) — using the same
    name as the argMin's own input column as an alias made ClickHouse's
    query analyzer reject the query ("cannot use aggregate function alias
    inside another aggregate function"); renamed to the closest non-
    colliding name to keep the query valid.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.

NODE lead_detail_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        MIN(timestamp) AS first_seen,
        MAX(timestamp) AS last_seen,
        countIf(event_type = '$pageview') AS pageviews,
        countIf(event_type = '$conversion') AS conversions,
        SUM(CASE WHEN event_type = '$conversion' THEN toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) ELSE 0 END) AS total_revenue,
        argMin(COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_source, ''), NULLIF(first_touch_source, ''), 'direct'), timestamp) AS source,
        argMin(COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_medium, ''), NULLIF(first_touch_medium, ''), 'none'), timestamp) AS medium,
        argMin(COALESCE(NULLIF(ai_source, ''), ''), timestamp) AS ai_source,
        argMin(country, timestamp) AS country,
        argMin(page_url, timestamp) AS first_page_url,
        argMin(first_touch_campaign, timestamp) AS campaign,
        argMin(first_touch_source, timestamp) AS ft_source,
        argMin(first_touch_medium, timestamp) AS ft_medium,
        COUNT(DISTINCT toDate(timestamp)) AS active_days
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND distinct_id = {{ String(distinct_id, required=True) }}
    GROUP BY distinct_id
    LIMIT 1

TYPE endpoint
